#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:4
msgid ":index:`Profile Options <configuration; profiles, profiles; option>`"
msgstr ":index:`Options de profil <configuration; profils, profils; option>`"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:6
msgid ""
"As of version 2.7, Picard supports multiple profiles that can quickly switch "
"between option settings. This page allows for the management of those user-"
"defined option profiles."
msgstr ""
"A partir de la version 2.7, Picard supporte plusieurs profils qui permettent "
"de passer rapidement d'une option à l'autre. Cette page permet la gestion de "
"ces profils d'options définis par l'utilisateur."

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:19
msgid ""
"Initially, the list of profiles will be empty. To create a new profile click "
"on the :guilabel:`New` button. This will create a profile with no options "
"selected for the profile to manage. To rename the profile, right-click on "
"the profile name and select the :menuselection:`\"Rename profile\"` command."
msgstr ""
"Initialement, la liste des profils sera vide. Pour créer un nouveau profil, "
"cliquez sur le bouton :guilabel:`Nouveau`. Cela créera un profil sans aucune "
"option sélectionnée pour le profil à gérer. Pour renommer le profil, faites "
"un clic droit sur le nom du profil et sélectionnez la "
"commande :menuselection:`\"Renommer le profil\"`."

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:21
msgid ""
"The options that the profile is to manage are selected from the list in the "
"right-hand pane. Options can be selected either by group or individually. "
"The groups can be expanded to see the individual options belonging to that "
"group."
msgstr ""
"Les options que le profil doit gérer sont sélectionnées dans la liste du "
"volet de droite. Les options peuvent être sélectionnées par groupe ou "
"individuellement. Les groupes peuvent être développés pour voir les options "
"individuelles appartenant à ce groupe."

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:23
msgid ""
"The profile stack order can be rearranged either by selecting a profile and "
"using the up and down arrow buttons below the list, or by dragging the "
"profile to a new position in the stack. Profiles are enabled when the box "
"beside the profile's name is checked."
msgstr ""
"L'ordre de la pile de profils peut être réorganisé soit en sélectionnant un "
"profil et en utilisant les boutons fléchés haut et bas sous la liste, soit "
"en faisant glisser le profil vers une nouvelle position dans la pile. Les "
"profils sont activés lorsque la case située à côté du nom du profil est "
"cochée."

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:25
msgid ""
"Changes made to a profile's options settings, enabled status, or position in "
"the profile stack will be reflected in the option settings displayed on the "
"other pages. Options that are controlled by an enabled profile will be shown "
"as highlighted. Hovering your cursor over the highlighted option will "
"identify which profile currently controls the setting. Settings are always "
"displayed based on the first enabled profile in the profile stack, which "
"corresponds to the setting that will be used during processing."
msgstr ""
"Les modifications apportées aux paramètres d'options d'un profil, à son "
"statut d'activation ou à sa position dans la pile de profils seront "
"reflétées dans les paramètres d'options affichés sur les autres pages. Les "
"options contrôlées par un profil activé apparaissent en surbrillance. Si "
"vous passez votre curseur sur l'option en surbrillance, vous saurez quel "
"profil contrôle actuellement ce paramètre. Les paramètres sont toujours "
"affichés en fonction du premier profil activé dans la pile de profils, qui "
"correspond au paramètre qui sera utilisé pendant le traitement."

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:29
msgid ""
"It is important to understand that when you click the :guilabel:`Make It So!"
"` button **all** of the option settings on **all** pages will be saved. If "
"an option is managed by one or more profiles that are currently enabled, the "
"option will be highlighted and it will be saved to the **first** enabled "
"profile in the profile stack that manages the option. If there are no "
"enabled profiles that manage the option, the option will not be highlighted "
"and it will be saved to the \"user settings\" profile which is the user's "
"normal settings, contains all options, is at the bottom of the profile "
"stack, and is always enabled. The \"user settings\" profile cannot be "
"modified and is not shown in the profile management page."
msgstr ""
"Il est important de comprendre que lorsque vous cliquez sur le "
"bouton :guilabel:`Faites-le donc!` **tous** les paramètres des options sur "
"**toutes** les pages seront enregistrés. Si une option est gérée par un ou "
"plusieurs profils actuellement activés, l'option sera mise en surbrillance "
"et sera enregistrée dans le **premier** profil activé de la pile de profils "
"qui gère l'option. Si aucun profil activé ne gère l'option, celle-ci ne sera "
"pas mise en surbrillance et sera enregistrée dans le profil \"paramètres "
"utilisateur\", qui correspond aux paramètres normaux de l'utilisateur, "
"contient toutes les options, se trouve au bas de la pile de profils et est "
"toujours activé. Le profil \"paramètres utilisateur\" ne peut pas être "
"modifié et n'apparaît pas dans la page de gestion des profils."

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:33
msgid ""
":index:`Backing Up and Sharing Profiles <profiles; backing up and sharing>`"
msgstr ""
":index:`Sauvegarde et partage des profils <profils; sauvegarde et partage>`"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:35
msgid ""
"You have the ability to export option profiles for backup purposes or to "
"share with others, and import option profiles previously exported."
msgstr ""
"Vous avez la possibilité d'exporter des profils d'options à des fins de "
"sauvegarde ou pour les partager avec d'autres personnes, ainsi que "
"d'importer des profils d'options précédemment exportés."

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:39
msgid ":index:`Exporting a profile definition <profiles; exporting>`"
msgstr ":index:`Exportation d'une définition de profil <profils; exportation>`"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:41
msgid ""
"When you click the :guilabel:`Export` button, the currently selected "
"(highlighted) profile can be output to a file. The export contains the "
"following information:"
msgstr ""
"Lorsque vous cliquez sur le bouton :guilabel:`Exporter`, le profil "
"actuellement sélectionné (mis en surbrillance) peut être exporté vers un "
"fichier. L'exportation contient les informations suivantes :"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:43
msgid "title of the profile"
msgstr "titre du profil"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:44
msgid "unique identifier assigned to the profile"
msgstr "identifiant unique attribué au profil"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:45
msgid "version of the profile export format used"
msgstr "version du format d'exportation de profil utilisée"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:46
msgid "version of Picard that created the profile export"
msgstr "version de Picard qui a généré l'exportation du profil"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:47
msgid "date that the profile was exported"
msgstr "date à laquelle le profil a été exporté"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:48
msgid "list of which settings are controlled by the profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:49
msgid "values of the settings controlled by the profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:51
msgid "You will first be asked to select the mode for the export."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:65
msgid "The choices for the export mode are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:67
msgid ""
"**Share**: All sensitive data such as account identification, passwords and "
"directory paths will be excluded from the export. This option is the "
"default, and should be used for any exports that you plan to make public or "
"share with others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:68
msgid ""
"**Backup**: Nothing will be excluded from the export. This should **only** "
"be selected for personal backup copies of your profiles that are not shared "
"with others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:70
msgid ""
"Once you have confirmed your choice of export mode, a file browser dialog "
"will open to allow you to select the directory and file name of the output "
"file. The profile exports are saved as ``*.toml`` files, which can be viewed "
"or modified with a text editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:72
msgid ""
"You can also export a profile in \"Share\" mode to the clipboard from the "
"context menu displayed when you right-click on the profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:84
#, fuzzy
msgid ":index:`Importing a profile definition <profiles; importing>`"
msgstr ":index:`Options de profil <configuration; profils, profils; option>`"

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:86
msgid ""
"To import a profile definition, you click the :guilabel:`Import` button. "
"This allows you to import the profile either from a profile export file, or "
"from a profile definition currently in the clipboard. If importing from a "
"file, a file browser dialog will open to allow you to select the file to "
"import."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:88
msgid ""
"Once the import source has been selected, Picard will verify that the import "
"is a valid profile definition. If it is valid, a new profile based on the "
"profile definition imported will be added at the top of your list of "
"profiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:92
msgid ""
"When importing a profile definition, if there is already a profile with the "
"same name in your list, you are prompted as to whether you want to create a "
"new copy or overwrite the existing profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:102
msgid ""
"If you choose to create a copy, the new profile will be added with a copy "
"number appended to the title, such as \"ByeByeWin (2)\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:104
msgid ""
"When you import a profile, you are also prompted as to whether you want the "
"new profile to be enabled after import."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_profiles.rst:109
msgid ""
"Please see the :doc:`../usage/option_profiles` section for a detailed "
"explanation of the profile system."
msgstr ""
"Veuillez consulter la section :doc:`../usage/option_profiles` pour une "
"explication détaillée du système de profils."
